jxl_lossless_band_2026-08-28.tsv — re-measure of the whole-image (global-tree)
lossless working set that `heuristics::estimate_encode` models as
`input + fixed(e) + bpp(e) * px`, after the August 2026 memory reductions had
left the 2026-08-01 anchors (base 92 / e6 235 / tree 540 / e10 620 B/px, from a
490 B/px 12 MP e7 cell) 3-5x stale-high — the "whole-image band is stale-high"
finding of the 2026-08-27 sectioned sweep.

Sources (real content, three classes): photo = imazen-26 1403 nature 4000x3000
sdr PNG and its top-left crops 64², 256², 1024², 2048², 3840x2160; imac =
gb82-sc imac_dark.png 2940x1912 (full palette + patches screenshot); reddit =
qoi-benchmark screenshot_web/reddit.com.png 1313x8008 and its 1313x4096 crop.
Efforts 5-10 (e10 photo only, to 4 MP), threads=1, SectionedTrees::Off
(global tree). Host: mac aarch64 laptop, release mem_probe.

Marginal B/px (peak_live - live_pre, per pixel):
  e5 : photo 73.1 (1 MP) / 70.3 (12 MP); imac 66.7; reddit 66.7
  e6 : photo 79.4 / 72.3; imac 62.2; reddit 67.8
  e7 : photo 105.5 / 98.1 / 96.4 / 94.6 (1 / 4 / 8.3 / 12 MP); imac 85.6; reddit 86.6 / 85.6
  e8 : photo 114.1 / 100.2 (1 / 12 MP); imac 87.3; reddit 87.9
  e9 : photo 141.3 / 121.2 / 127.0 / 129.5; imac 137.7; reddit 129.7 / 130.2
  e10: photo 236.0 (1 MP) / 129.1 (4 MP)  — a ~150 MB size-independent multi-seed term
Intercepts (256² cells, marginal): e7 20.5 MB, e8 25.9 MB, e9 67.3 MB, e10 67.3 MB
(64² e7: 6.0 MB).
Alpha (rgba - rgb marginal): e7 +37.3 B/px (1 MP) / +33.5 (8.3 MP); e9 +62.8 / +27.1.

New constants (heuristics.rs): LOSSLESS_BPP_BASE 92 (kept), _E6 92 (was 235),
_TREE (e7-e8) 128 (was 540), _E9 160 (new), _E10 160 (was 620) with
lossless_fixed_overhead(e): 16 MiB (e<=6) / 24 MiB (e7-8) / 64 MiB (e9) /
160 MiB (e>=10); LOSSLESS_BPP_ALPHA 72 (was 230). Every cell is TYP-covered and
tight (< 2.5x) at >= 1 MP (heuristics::tests::
lossless_estimate_covers_measured_cells_2026_08_28).

Consequences: `LosslessConfig::estimate_encode` and the `Auto` memory-pressure
gate drop ~4x for e7-e9 (12 MP e7 TYP 6.4 GB -> 1.6 GB, measured peak_live 1.14
GB); at the 8 GiB lossless default cap, whole-image e7 admits up to ~65 MP
(was ~15.7 MP), so the tests that pinned the default-cap behaviour moved to
49 MP (path-aware cap relation), 21 MP under an explicit 2 GiB cap (Auto
engages sectioned / Off rejects) and 72 MP (default-cap rejection under Off).
